{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1024","id":4956525987,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJgfwyc8AAAABJ26Vow","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1024","diff_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1024.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1024.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1024","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1024/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1024/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1024/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/statuses/f419ea8f82c8bd16a777cfc3bf6cbf8c85be60dd","number":1024,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(scripts): retain terminal diagnostics and join cancelled profiles","user":{"login":"tangtaoit","id":3895878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTU4Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3895878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit","html_url":"https://github.com/tangtaoit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Cloud RC failures could lose worker failure samples and terminal status, discard oversized metric results, or query a window after the workload had already stopped. This change retains bounded terminal diagnostics, partitions fixed metric queries under shared time/byte limits, and binds their window to the terminal report. Missing or partial evidence stays explicit and never changes the workload verdict.\n\nThe full regression also exposed a profile-helper cancellation race: a signal between starting curl and registering its PID could leave an HTTP request alive after the helper reported interruption. The helper now defers signal cleanup through complete request registration, then cancels and joins its owned requests. Empty cleanup arrays also work with Bash 3 nounset.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Terminal collection: 20 Python methods / 79 process scenarios passed locally, including red-first reproduction and independent boundary probes. Both review axes have no open findings. A fixture-only optimization preserves all cases and their semantic results.\n- Profile cancellation: 9 deterministic process scenarios (before launch, first request registration, second-node registration × HUP/INT/TERM) failed before the fix and passed afterward. The first focused validation passed all 15 top-level tests / 38 PASS records; original tests and time limits are unchanged. Both independent review axes report no findings.\n- Original head c91e37b4: Linux default/E2E/performance passed, but scripts hit the original 600-second outer timeout. That failure remains retained.\n- Head 2cc562fa: Linux default/E2E/performance passed; collector tests passed and the full scripts command completed in 575.954 seconds, but the original profile-interrupt assertion failed because server 2 still had an active request. That first failure is retained and led to the deterministic repair above.\n- Head 44de9452: first-attempt Linux default, migration/messaging E2E and performance checks passed. The full scripts command hit the unchanged 600-second outer deadline (600.100 seconds recorded, cleanup verified with no remaining processes), with no failed test assertion. All nine new registration/cancellation cases and the original interruption test passed; terminal retention and other pending tests did not finish, so the scripts gate remains failed. Run 39664872167 and performance run 39664872153 are retained. No failed CI was rerun, no deadline or concurrency limit was relaxed, and this PR remains draft. Cross-generation timing analysis found little outer-budget margin; lock-admission waits remain an inference from event intervals and source, without observed acquisition timestamps.\n\n- Current head f419ea8f removes two unused real builds from one controlled Start fixture through existing tool inputs and moves that real-process case into the integration tier. The same serial scratch first failed the no-extra-build postcondition with two successful Go builds, then passed with zero; all original operation, artifact, permission and state assertions were preserved. The first related default 11 and integration 15 tests passed, and both independent review axes found no issues. This measured local work reduction does not predict Linux savings or establish a complete scripts pass. The first unchanged Linux candidate/performance gates for this head are pending.\n\nThe cloud message-loss root cause remains unconfirmed. This is diagnostic retention and cancellation cleanup, not a claimed repair of that historical loss. No cloud resources, production keys, stable activation, or release publication are included. Product cmd/internal/pkg and dependency objects remain unchanged.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T18:36:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T20:28:01Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"0c575fd63bcf8164332ca28053039f8fdf84137f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"WuKongIM:codex/v3-rc-terminal-evidence","ref":"codex/v3-rc-te